    "parts": [
      {
        "id": 6497,
        "quiz_id": 6384,
        "passage": 4,
        "title": "Listening Passage 4",
        "sort": 4,
        "content": "Listening Passage 4",
        "explanations": [],
        "questions": [],
        "vocabs": [
          {
            "id": 891836,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 891837,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "For my project on invertebrates, I chose to study tardigrades.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 76.685005,
                  "from": 72.125,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 891848,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "These are microscopic - or to be more precise - near-microscopic animals.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 81.645004,
                  "from": 76.925,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 891858,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "There are well over a thousand known species of these tiny animals, which belong to the phylum Tardigrada.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 89.27,
                  "from": 82.045006,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 891876,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Most tardigrades range in length from 0.05 to 1 millimetre, though the largest species can grow to be 1.2 millimetres in length.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 101.03,
                  "from": 89.909996,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 891899,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They are also sometimes called ’water bears’: ’water’ because that’s where they thrive best, and ’bear’ because of the way they move.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 110.385,
                  "from": 101.905,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 891922,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "’Moss piglet’ is another name for tardigrades because of the way they look when viewed from the front.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 117.770004,
                  "from": 111.025,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 891941,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They were first discovered in Germany in 1773 by Johann Goeze, who coined the name Tardigrada.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 126.73,
                  "from": 118.17,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 891958,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 891959,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "As I say, there are many different species of tardigrade - too many to describe here - but, generally speaking, the different species share similar physical traits.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 138.97499,
                  "from": 127.935,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 891985,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They have a body which is short and also rounded - a bit like a barrel - and the body comprises four segments.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 148.75,
                  "from": 139.55,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892004,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Each segment has a pair of legs, at the end of which are between four and eight sharp claws.",
                "youpass_pick_words": [
                  "segment"
                ],
                "meta": {
                  "to": 155.93501,
                  "from": 149.06999,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892023,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I should also say that some species don’t have any claws; what they have are discs, and these work by means of suction.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 165.695,
                  "from": 156.255,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892047,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They enable the tardigrade to cling on to surfaces or to grip its prey.",
                "youpass_pick_words": [
                  "grip"
                ],
                "meta": {
                  "to": 171.87001,
                  "from": 166.35,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892061,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Within the body, there are no lungs, or any organs for breathing at all.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 176.91,
                  "from": 172.19,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892075,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Instead, oxygen and also blood are transported in a fluid that fills the cavity of the body.",
                "youpass_pick_words": [
                  "cavity"
                ],
                "meta": {
                  "to": 184.74501,
                  "from": 177.47,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 892092,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 892093,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "As far as the tardigrade’s head is concerned, the best way I can describe this is that it looks rather strange - a bit squashed even - though many of the websites I looked at described its appearance as cute, which isn’t exactly very scientific.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 202.40001,
                  "from": 185.785,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892136,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The tardigrade’s mouth is a kind of tube that can open outwards to reveal teeth-like structures known as ’stylets’.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 211.315,
                  "from": 202.8,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892155,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "These are sharp enough to pierce plant or animal cells.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 215.475,
                  "from": 211.795,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 892165,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 892166,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "So, where are tardigrades found?",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 219.235,
                  "from": 216.595,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892172,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Well, they live in every part of the world, in a variety of habitats: most commonly, on the bed of a lake, or on many kinds of plants or in very wet environments.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 232.29001,
                  "from": 219.395,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892202,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "There’s been some interesting research which has found that tardigrades are capable of surviving radiation and very high pressure, and they’re also able to withstand temperatures as cold as -200 degrees celsius, or highs of more than 148 degrees celsius, which is incredibly hot.",
                "youpass_pick_words": [
                  "radiation"
                ],
                "meta": {
                  "to": 247.39499,
                  "from": 232.84999,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892246,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "It has been said that tardigrades could survive long after human beings have been wiped out, even in the event of an asteroid hitting the earth.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 269.52502,
                  "from": 256.14,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 892273,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 892274,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "If conditions become too extreme and tardigrades are at risk of drying out, they enter a state called cryptobiosis.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 278.245,
                  "from": 270.165,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892293,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They curl into a ball, called a tun - that’s T-U-N - by retracting their head and legs, and their metabolism drops to less than one percent of normal levels.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 281.06,
                  "from": 278.9,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892320,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They can remain like this until they are re-introduced to water, when they will come back to life in a matter of a few hours.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 293.815,
                  "from": 291.575,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892344,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "While in a state of cryptobiosis, tardigrades produce a protein that protects their DNA.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 306.45502,
                  "from": 299.575,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892357,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In 2016, scientists revived two tardigrades that had been tuns for more than 30 years.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 314.43,
                  "from": 307.31,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892373,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "There was a report that, in 1948, a 120-year-old tun was revived, but this experiment has never been repeated.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 325.015,
                  "from": 315.06998,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892391,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "There are currently several tests taking place in space to determine how long tardigrades might be able to survive there.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 334.055,
                  "from": 325.495,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892412,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I believe the record so far is 10 days.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 337.335,
                  "from": 334.695,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 892422,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 892423,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In terms of their diet, tardigrades consume liquids in order to survive.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 346.92,
                  "from": 340.76,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892436,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Although they have teeth, they don’t use these for chewing.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 350.76,
                  "from": 347.32,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892447,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They suck the juices from moss, or extract fluid from seaweed, but some species prey on other tardigrades, from other species or within their own.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 362.725,
                  "from": 351.36502,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892471,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I suppose this isn’t surprising, given that tardigrades are mainly comprised of liquid and are coated with a type of gel.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 371.62,
                  "from": 363.54,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 892492,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 892493,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Finally, I’d like to mention the conservation status of tardigrades.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 376.66,
                  "from": 372.58,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892504,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "It is estimated that they have been in existence for approximately half a billion years and, in that time, they have survived five mass extinctions.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 387.89502,
                  "from": 377.415,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892529,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "So, it will probably come as no surprise to you that tardigrades have not been evaluated by the International Union for Conservation of Nature and are not on any endangered list.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 401.00998,
                  "from": 388.375,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 892561,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Some researchers have described them as thriving.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 405.16998,
                  "from": 401.65,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 892569,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 892570,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Does anyone have any questions they’d like to ask?",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 409.665,
                  "from": 406.225,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
